==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|masculinus||masculine|lang=la}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# A social theory or political movement supporting the [[equality]] of both sexes in all aspects of public and private life; specifically, a theory or movement that argues that legal and social restrictions on males must be removed in order to bring about such [[equality]].
# Advocacy of the [[right]]s of men; (sometimes implicitly) [[anti-feminism]], because masculinists protest modern female privileges, the discrimination of men and the oppression of men caused by the excesses of the feminist movement.

